### Auth: log in as acme's seeded admin. Reading the audit log is ADMIN only.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "email": "admin@acme.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("acmeToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Auth: acme's seeded SUPPORT user, for the 403 check below.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "acme",
  "email": "support@acme.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("supportToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Auth: a second tenant, for the isolation check.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "tenantId": "demo",
  "email": "admin@demo.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("demoToken", response.body.token);
%}

### Auth: the platform administrator.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/auth/token
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "platform@subscriptionhub.test",
  "password": "subscriptionhub"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("platformToken", response.body.token);
%}


### Setup: something to audit. Codes and email embed a timestamp so the file can be re-run.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/products
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

{
  "code": "audit-product-{{$timestamp}}",
  "name": "Audit Product"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("auditProductCode", response.body.code);
%}

### Setup: plan (records PLAN_CREATED with the price in data)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/plans
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

{
  "productCode": "{{auditProductCode}}",
  "code": "audit-plan-{{$timestamp}}",
  "name": "Audit Plan",
  "intervalUnit": "MONTH",
  "amountCents": 4900,
  "currency": "USD"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("auditPlanCode", response.body.code);
%}

### Setup: customer (records CUSTOMER_CREATED with no email or name in data)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

{
  "email": "audit-{{$timestamp}}@acme.test",
  "name": "Audit Customer"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("auditCustomerId", response.body.id);
%}

### Setup: subscription (records SUBSCRIPTION_CREATED)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

{
  "customerId": "{{auditCustomerId}}",
  "planCode": "{{auditPlanCode}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("auditSubscriptionId", response.body.id);
%}

### Pause (records SUBSCRIPTION_PAUSED, data.from = ACTIVE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{auditSubscriptionId}}/pause
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### Resume twice: the first records SUBSCRIPTION_RESUMED, the second is 409 and records nothing
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{auditSubscriptionId}}/resume
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/subscriptions/{{auditSubscriptionId}}/resume
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}


### Tenant timeline: newest first (expects 200; actorType USER, actorId = the admin's user id, requestId set)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### One subscription's history (expects RESUMED, PAUSED, CREATED, and only one RESUMED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit-events?entityType=SUBSCRIPTION&entityId={{auditSubscriptionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### Paged (expects size 2, totalElements >= 3)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit-events?entityType=SUBSCRIPTION&entityId={{auditSubscriptionId}}&size=2
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### Incomplete filter: entityType without entityId (expects 400 AUDIT_FILTER_INCOMPLETE)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit-events?entityType=SUBSCRIPTION
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}

### Not an admin: SUPPORT reads everything else, but not the audit log (expects 403 ACCESS_DENIED)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{supportToken}}

### No token (expects 401)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit-events

### Tenant isolation: acme's subscription id under demo (expects 200 with an empty content list, not acme's events)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit-events?entityType=SUBSCRIPTION&entityId={{auditSubscriptionId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{demoToken}}

### Tenant isolation: a platform token on the tenant endpoint (expects 403; it names no tenant)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}


### Platform view of acme's log (expects 200, the same events as the tenant timeline)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/tenants/acme/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### Platform lifecycle: deactivate then activate demo, then read demo's log
### (expects TENANT_ACTIVATED and TENANT_DEACTIVATED with actorType PLATFORM_ADMIN).
### Repeating a deactivate is a no-op and adds no event.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/tenants/demo/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/tenants/demo/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

###
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/tenants/demo/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/tenants/demo/audit-events?entityType=TENANT&entityId=demo
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### Platform view of an unknown tenant (expects 404, not an empty page)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/tenants/no-such-tenant/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{platformToken}}

### A tenant admin on the platform endpoint (expects 403)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/platform/tenants/acme/audit-events
Authorization: Bearer {{acmeToken}}
